vatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2436340?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prvak","html_url":"https://github.com/prvak","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prvak/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prvak/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prvak/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prvak/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prvak/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prvak/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prvak/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prvak/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prvak/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-05T13:55:09Z","updated_at":"2026-05-05T13:55:09Z","body":"> That might be difficult, might be difficult to identify that this is calling this and not an actual resource\n\nWould it be too difficult to get an error when I define a static function with the same name as an existing method within `GDScript`? Such a function would always be replaced by the existing `GDScript` method. Either automatically by the engine loading the script as a `GDScript` instance or by loading it manually with `preload`. \n\n> it might also be something you want to do\n\nI am not sure that I understand what you mean by this. Why would I want to write a function that is ignored by the engine? I don't see any scenario where my custom static function would be actually executed.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4379932666/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4380166074","html_url":"