_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prvak","html_url":"https://github.com/prvak","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prvak/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prvak/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prvak/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prvak/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prvak/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prvak/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prvak/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prvak/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prvak/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-05T18:14:13Z","updated_at":"2026-05-05T18:14:13Z","body":"Overriding native methods used to behave the same way. They were not executed and there was no error.  \n- https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/55024\n\nToday, we have a nice error message saying that it is not possible to override native method.\n\nI wish something similar were possible for static methods and GDScript class. I understand that technically there is no method to conflict with. In practice the conflict exists and is very obscure and hard to debug.\n\nJust to be clear, I have no problem renaming the conflicting static method in my code. The problem is that I have no way of knowing that I should rename it :)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4381840740/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]